 my my dishes would taste horrible.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: How did that happen?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: If I put in a half ounce of salt instead of a quarter ounce, it alters everything.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: True. I used to cook more often when I was in college. Sometimes when I put in a little less water, it changed the sauce. But I would still eat it."}, {"time": "41000", "image": "engenn6le03ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yeah, when I was in culinary school, my mom used to help me a lot. We would experiment with how to use various ingredients.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: Nice.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I used follow recipes very closely, but now I have a sense of how much is enough.<br />"}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 2, "_data": []}]}]}